Again, there’s far too little information.
If the estimated dependence is small, than the predictions will essentially be the common mean. For some problems, variations in the decimals can be highly significant. For others, less so. The estimates need to be taken I context, and not only the means but also the std.dev <http://std.dev>. and quantiles are informative. You need to show more of the actual numbers and parameter estimates.

Finn

