As far as loading R with a CUDA BLAS installation goes, it's as simple as overloading the shared object and passing a config file when opening R:

LD_PRELOAD=/usr/.../libnvblas.so NVBLAS_CONFIG_FILE=/path/to/some/nv.conf R

This would overload the BLAS functions with the ones provided by CUDA.

