Here is the  linking for the CentOS7 build, which uses

	[hrue@centos70 build64]$ rpm -qa|grep glibc
	glibc-2.17-260.el7_6.3.x86_64

works well for me

g++ -O2 -msse2 -mtune=generic -ftracer -pipe   -std=c11 -fopenmp
-I/usr/include/R -DINLA_LIBR  -o inla src/inla.o
src/dictionary.o  src/iniparser.o  src/strlib.o src/my-fix.o src/sha1.o
src/spde.o src/spde2.o src/spde3.o src/eval.o src/interpol.o src/re.o
src/ar.o src/bessel.o src/pc-priors.o src/R-interface.o src/fgn.o
src/quantile-regression.o src/my.o src/stochvol.o  -
L/home/hrue/builds/build64/local/lib  -L/usr/lib -lRmath
-L/usr/lib/R/lib -lR -L/home/hrue/builds/build64/local/lib -lGMRFLib
-L/home/hrue/builds/build64/local/lib  -static-libstdc++ -static-libgcc
-lgsl  -ltaucs -lpardiso                     -lz -lgfortran -lamd
-lmuparser -L/usr/lib64/R/lib -lRmath -lR 	            -
L/opt/intel/mkl/lib/intel64_lin -Wl,--no-as-needed -lmkl_intel_lp64
-lmkl_intel_thread -lmkl_core                     -
L/opt/intel/lib/intel64_lin/ -liomp5 -lpthread -lm -ldl -Wl,--whole-
archive -lpthread -Wl,--no-whole-archive -lm

gives

[hrue@centos70 build64]$ local/bin/inla.mkl.run -m pardiso

SUCCESS: PARDISO IS INSTALLED AND WORKING

